Command:
cd magnetgoogo-app && npx tsc --noEmit && node scripts/app-adversarial-tests.mjs

Result:
TypeScript PASS, then Node ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND for src/core/infoHash imported from types.ts.

Root cause:
The repository's direct Node TypeScript test runtime requires explicit `.ts` extensions for local ESM imports. The new module was imported as `./infoHash`.

Impact:
Test-runtime module resolution only. TypeScript compilation passed; production logic was not executed by this failed run.

Fix:
Use explicit `./infoHash.ts` imports and rerun TypeScript plus adversarial tests.
